{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q009_heme_bundle_fold_not_homology","answer":"No. In SCOPe release 2.08 (the stable release; the current periodic update was not inspected for these nodes), the three groups share only the fold-level architecture. SCOPe places all three in fold f.21, "Heme-binding four-helical bundle", but in three different superfamilies: f.21.1 "Transmembrane di-heme cytochromes" (sunid 81342), f.21.2 "Fumarate reductase respiratory complex transmembrane subunits" (sunid 81343), and f.21.3 "Respiratory nitrate reductase 1 gamma chain" (sunid 103501, with its family f.21.3.1, sunid 103502). Because SCOPe does not place them in one superfamily, it asserts no superfamily-level common ancestry among them. The shared heme-binding four-helical-bundle architecture is a fold-level structural similarity, which SCOPe does not treat as evidence of common ancestry.

The SCOPe hierarchy does not show that these groups are nonhomologous, analogous, or convergent. Different superfamilies within one fold only mean SCOPe makes no positive superfamily-level homology assertion. A claim of shared ancestry, or of independent origin, would need evidence outside hierarchy placement, such as a sequence or structural alignment with inspected residue correspondence. I did not retrieve any such evidence.

Limits: I did not query the children of f.21.1 (sunid 81342), so its family composition is unverified here. I did not retrieve the /annotations or /homology caveat records for these nodes, and I did not check domain-level (sid) assignments. The exact query "nitrate reductase gamma" returned no results; the gamma-chain node surfaced only under the broader query "nitrate reductase". I make no claim about substrates, redox partners, or catalytic function beyond the SCOPe descriptors retrieved above.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=cytochrome%20b&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=fumarate%20reductase&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=nitrate%20reductase%20gamma&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=nitrate%20reductase&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=di-heme&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=transmembrane%20cytochrome%20b&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81344","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81344/children?limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81373","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81373/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/56910/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/103501/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/103501/children?limit=20"]}]}
